# Git commits

The user commits their own work. **Do not** run `git commit`, stage files for commit, or offer to commit as a default follow-up.

Only create a commit when the user **explicitly** asks (e.g. "commit this", "create a commit").

When asked to commit, follow the repo's commit message style and never commit secrets (`.env.local`, credentials, etc.).
